## 7. Reading pgbench output correctly

```
transaction type: <builtin: TPC-B (sort of)>
scaling factor: 50
query mode: simple
number of clients: 10
number of threads: 2
duration: 90 s
number of transactions actually processed: 34521
latency average = 26.073 ms
tps = 383.552341 (including connections establishing)
```

- **`tps`** — the single headline number for before/after comparison.
- **`latency average`** — mean, so a few very bad outliers can hide inside a
  reasonable-looking average. This is why `-P 5` matters more than the final
  summary — the interval printouts reveal spikes the average smooths over.
- Add `--latency-histogram` (newer pgbench versions) or note the per-interval
  latency numbers from `-P 5` if you want to show variance, not just the mean,
  in your before/after report.

